From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Lemenkov <lemenkov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:27:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/41] Escape "-" in topic permission variables

The CVE-2026-44838 fix escapes regex metacharacters in expanded topic
permission variables, but not "-". Inside a "[...]" character class
"-" forms a range, so a client ID such as "a-z" substituted into a
template like "^[{client_id}]-sensors$" still widens the pattern.

Upstream fixed this in eb7e0e2ad6 ("Improve `rabbit_re`, adopt it in
more places"), which moves the escaping into a new rabbit_re:escape/1
and adds "-" to the escaped set. 4.0.9 has no rabbit_re, so add "-" to
escape_regex_char/1 directly and port the upstream test case.

Fixes CVE-2026-67407.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Peter Lemenkov <lemenkov@gmail.com>
---
 deps/rabbit/src/rabbit_auth_backend_internal.erl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/deps/rabbit/src/rabbit_auth_backend_internal.erl b/deps/rabbit/src/rabbit_auth_backend_internal.erl
index d55956f9b6..3f1ff6322c 100644
--- a/deps/rabbit/src/rabbit_auth_backend_internal.erl
+++ b/deps/rabbit/src/rabbit_auth_backend_internal.erl
@@ -197,7 +197,7 @@ escape_regex_char(C)
   when C =:= $\\; C =:= $^; C =:= $$; C =:= $.;
        C =:= $|; C =:= $?; C =:= $*; C =:= $+;
        C =:= $(; C =:= $); C =:= $[; C =:= $];
-       C =:= ${; C =:= $} ->
+       C =:= ${; C =:= $}; C =:= $- ->
     <<$\\, C>>;
 escape_regex_char(C) ->
     <<C>>.
